      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Bixie Warfront [zone=941]\n**Who:**\n- Commander Zavrus [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 100\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Stone Hive Orders [item=113768]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Jeslellathina [ _The Feral Spark_]\n- Scout Reneza [npc=44605]\n- Warden Lorenz [npc=44374]\n- Warden Lorenz [npc=44375]\n- Warden Lorenz [npc=44373]\n- a barricade guard [npc=45422]\n- a bruised merchant [npc=44709]\n- a forgettable tenant [npc=44713]\n- a frightened bixie [npc=44951]\n- a honey bender [npc=44758]\n- a honey bender [npc=44716]\n- a path protector [npc=44720]\n- a quiet tenant [npc=44725]\n- a river guardian [npc=44727]\n- a river guardian [npc=44770]\n- a spider hunter [npc=44925]\n- a supply guardian [npc=44733]\n- an investigator - Bixie Warfront [npc=44740]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Crizlyna #1: Assault the Main Hive [quest=7269]\n- Crizlyna #2: Jacyll's Jailbreak [quest=7270]\n- Raid Expedition: Saving Jacyll [quest=7262]\n- Saving Jacyll [quest=7261]\n- Snazlieu #1: Espionage Starts at Home [quest=7263]\n- Snazlieu #2: Always Follow the Money [quest=7264]\n- Snazlieu #3: Working Overtime [quest=7265]\n- Yrelia #1: The Great Hunt [quest=7266]\n- Yrelia #2: They've Gone Too Far This Time [quest=7267]\n- Yrelia #3: They're Everywhere! [quest=7268]\n**Era:** | !Call of the Forsaken\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Oct 8 05:53:47 2013\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 |\n---\n\n**Call of the Forsaken Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is a solo task that begins with Commander Zavrus ( **map image**). She is a drakkin found in the Queen's Wet River bixie camp (from the Ethernere portal stone, head east up the ramp and just follow the ramp until you come to the queen's camp)._\n_Pre-Requisites for requesting:_\n\\- Level 85\n\\- Completed Ethernere Tainted West Karana tasks:\n\\-\\-\\- \"Overcoming the Cataclysm\"\n\\-\\-\\- \"Not of This World\"\n\\-\\-\\- \"Answering the Call\"\nYou say, 'Hail, Commander Zavrus'\nCommander Zavrus says 'Greetings. I don't suppose you are for hire, are you? I'm conducting an [investigation] of the recent militarization of the Stone Hive bixies. The Wet River bixies are trying to find the source of the music and sounds causing it, and I have a few people already helping, but it is not enough. Frislo here has done what he can, but while I am sympathetic with his plight, there are more lives at stake than just his brother Jacyll's.'\nYou say, 'I'll help with this investigation'\n_Without pre-requisites, you see:_\nCommander Zavrus says 'I don't think you can help me at this time.'\n_With pre-requisites, you see:_\nCommander Zavrus says 'I'm grateful for the help. With everyone else preparing for war, I've been low on resources to do anything for actually preventing war. I've been working with the Wet River bixies to learn more about this sound that drives the Stone Hive. It is likely some sort of magical source, but beyond that I don't know anything.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Bixies of War'.\nA strange sound is echoing through the caverns, and only the Wet River bixies' wax prevents others from succumbing to the strange effects. The Stone Hive is now on the move.\nAssist Commander Zavrus from Crescent Reach with the investigation into militarization of the Stone Hive bixies.\n\n---\n\n_Map points for \"bixiewarfront.txt\" map files:_\nP 440.3686, 43.4288, -80.3821, 240, 0, 0, 2, Stone\\_Hive\\_Order\nP 434.5842, 300.0411, -112.2936, 240, 0, 0, 2, Stone\\_Hive\\_Order\nP 1187.6378, 222.1013, -174.6282, 240, 0, 0, 2, Stone\\_Hive\\_Order\nP 817.3863, 222.4731, -183.3348, 240, 0, 0, 2, Stone\\_Hive\\_Order\n\n---\n\nSpeak to Scout Reneza 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Find Scout Reneza of the Wet River bixies. Zavrus believes that she may be able to help.\n_Scout Reneza ( **map image**) is found in the same camp._\nYou say, 'Hail, Scout Reneza'\nScout Reneza says 'Commander Zavrus has asked you to look into this? Very well. I will assist you, only because our interests coincide. The Stone Hive is no longer our ally. This music of war, rage, and fury does not affect us since we have protected ourselves with the [wax]. The wax will keep you sane as well. We'll need to find information from the Stone Hive members themselves to get any further in finding the source, however.'\nYou say, 'Wax?'\nScout Reneza says 'That vile sound. If we do not stop it soon, who knows what might happen next? If you'd like to help, contact the drakkin called Zavrus. She is a member of the Crescent Reach military.'\n\n---\n\nReturn to Commander Zavrus 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Inform Commander Zavrus of what you've learned.\nYou say, 'Hail, Commander Zavrus'\nCommander Zavrus says 'Reneza was helpful, I see. She did seem the reasonable sort. I think we should start by taking out some Stone Hive bixies and seeing if we can find any useful leads. I'll see what I can find out on my end.'\n\n---\n\nLocate clues by taking out Stone Hive bixies 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Find clues from Stone Hive bixies. Troopers, diggers, lancers, and soldiers may have information.\n_Kill bixies in the static (non-instanced) Bixie Warfront until you get an update. These include:_\na bustling digger\na frantic harvester\na resolute trooper\na vigilant soldier\nan edgy lancer\n_These spawn in the large clearing in the tunnel behind Naturalist Yrelia ( **map image** of Yrelia)._\na resolute trooper has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\na resolute trooper had some interesting information that completes part of the puzzle. Your victim has left behind a few clues: you found information that Warden Lorenz was the person who handled the prisoner Jacyll and some near-mad scribblings about a war march. It looks like you'll need to do more investigating, but first, you should let Zavrus know what you found out.\n\n---\n\nDiscuss the findings with Commander Zavrus 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Report your findings to Commander Zavrus.\nYou say, 'Hail, Commander Zavrus'\nCommander Zavrus says 'This is a good start. I haven't been able to get much done here, but I'll keep looking. In the meantime, I'll need you to follow up on this.'\n\n---\n\nInterrogate bixies 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\nThis is reported to update from \"a spider hunter\" that was standing next to Charlbroiled Chanon.\nFind information by killing bixies 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\nCollect Stone Hive Orders and give them to Commander Zavrus 0/5 (Bixie Warfront)\nDefeat Warden Lorenz to learn about Jacyll's fate 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Interrogate non-hostile bixies, defeat hostile bixies, collect Stone Hive orders, and find Warden Lorenz. Hostile bixies that may have information could include guards, protectors, investigators, or honey benders. Non-hostile bixies that may be willing to talk could include vendors, tenants, friendly hunters, or frightened bixies.\n_The above four steps can only be completed inside instances involving heroic adventures. Speak with Naturalist Yrelia, Snazlieu the Shadow, or Ambassador Crizlyna to initiate these tasks (they are shared tasks for 1-6 players -- a list of them can be found in **this progression writeup**). Note: All four steps are known to be updateable inside the \"Espionage Begins At Home\" instance._\n_For the \"interrogate\" step, just hail non-KOS bixies until you get an update:_\nYou say, 'Hail, a quiet tenant'\na quiet tenant says 'The song fills us all with strength and zeal. The warriors in particular have found great energy. There is a non-bixie playing it. Looks like one of the people of Crescent Reach.'\n_For the \"find information\" step, kill KOS guards, protectors, investigators, and honey benders until you get an update (these mob types are most common in heroic adventures involving the residences - see Snazlieu the Sneak to trigger these tasks):_\na supply guardian has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\na supply guardian had notes about the \"power of the drum\" on one of the corpses. There are references to the \"power it brings.\"\n_For the \"collect\" step, \"Stone Hive Orders\" are found as ground spawns inside bixie residences (trigger heroic adventures beginning with Snazlieu the Shadow to access their houses; this may also be possible in Ambassador Crizlyna's tasks, but this is not confirmed)._\n_Warden Lorenz can only be reached inside Heroic Adventures involving the residential district (those triggered by speaking with Snazlieu the Shadow). It's possible to invis to his location, kill him, and leave the zone without doing anything else. Note that he casts a 50' range AE for 40,000 damage (average amount of hitpoints, average DPS)._\n_For a map to the Warden's location, **click here** (he's west of the residences)._\nWarden Lorenz has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nWarden Lorenz's corpse buzzes pitifully and hits the ground.\nWarden Lorenz had a list of prisoners in a small journal. It appears Jacyll is a prisoner of some importance, but the exact reasons are not revealed. He is the Queen Bixie's personal prisoner.\n_Upon handing in the Stone Hive Orders, you see:_\nCommander Zavrus says 'Now these are fascinating. Thank you.'\n\n---\n\nDiscuss the revelations with Scout Reneza 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Report the results of your foray to Scout Reneza.\nYou say, 'Hail, Scout Reneza'\nScout Reneza says 'So the sound of the drum, that horrible music. That which we are protecting against, is made from a Stone Hive prisoner named Jacyll? I appreciate you sharing this information with us. You should tell the soldier from Crescent Reach your findings.'\n\n---\n\nGive your final report to Commander Zavrus 0/1 (Bixie Warfront)\n_Task Window Says:_ Give your final report to Commander Zavrus.\nYou say, 'Hail, Commander Zavrus'\nCommander Zavrus nods. 'It looks like Jacyll and this drum might be what's causing the bixie's behavior. This is incredibly serious. However, if we can stop him from playing this artifact and rescue him, we might be able to avoid a war. You've been an incredible help. Thank you.'\nYou've learned much. The Stone Hive bixies are being controlled by a magical drum played by Jacyll, a prisoner of the Stone Hive bixies. It will be necessary to free him to recover the drum and halt the march of war.\n_Rewards:_\nExperience (3-4 AAs at Level 100)\n262 platinum, 5 gold\n_(This task is repeatable with a 6-hour lockout - lockout from the time the task was requested.)_\n\n---\n\n**Precursor & Lore**\n_While not a part of this task or any progression, the Drakkin named Jeslellathina of Crescent Reach (found beneath the ladder that leads up to the new zone) has a few things to say about the Bixie Warfront:_\nYou say, 'Hail, Jeslellathina'\n[Jeslellathina] plays with a bit of flame wrapping around her knuckles as she says, 'Have you ever seen a [building burn], \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_?'\nYou say, 'Jeslellathina...'\nJeslellathina laughs, holds her flaming hand up to her mouth and blows a kiss of flame at you. She says playfully, 'Don't mock the name, honey. It's specifically chosen for its purpose, just like you've been.'\nYou say, 'A building burn?'\nJeslellathina looks up at you, confused by your answer. She asks again, 'Well, have you?'\nYou say, 'No...'\nJeslellathina snaps her hand shut with surprising force and snuffs the flame out. 'What a pity. You're really missing out. [Honeycomb] burns quite well, too, though.'\nYou say, 'Honeycomb?'\nJeslellathina says 'Oh, have you not heard already? I'd assumed everyone in Crescent Reach had by now; the gossip here is quite out of control. Well, we're here on a [rescue] mission.'\nYou say, 'Rescue?'\nJeslellathina says 'Jacyll, one of the finest bards I've ever heard, and a personal friend of mine, was kidnapped by the Stone Hive bixies. Thus, the [ladder]!'\nYou say, 'What's this ladder?'\nJeslellathina looks a little irritated that you require more explanation. She begins flicking flames off of her fingers as she recites, 'Attention, all brave adventures that set foot inside Crescent Reach's borders! The esteemed and well-respected bard, Jacyll, has been kidnapped by the Stone Hive Bixies and taken to their [underground camp].'\nYou say, 'What underground camp?'\nJeslellathina says 'Yes, yes. I was getting to that.' Jeslellathina takes a deep breath and continues drearily, 'Their newly excavated underground tunnel network can be accessed via a subterranean pathway and one super long ladder. The authorities of Crescent Reach can guarantee safe passage into the underground fortress, but assumes no [liability] for...'\nYou say, 'Liability?'\nJeslellathina's head snaps up like she fell asleep, smiles, and says, 'Oh yes, it'd be a shame to miss that part. As I was saying, Crescent Reach assumes no liability for any serious injuries, BEST FRIENDS, decapitations, life-threatening predicaments, BEAUTIFUL FLOWERS, diseases, bug bites, or HEAPING PILES OF TREASURE that may be acquired within [the cavern].'\nYou say, 'The cavern?'\nJeslellathina shoots spark into the sky and says, 'We've taken to calling it the Bixie Warfront, but there's really no official term for the place. It's just an extension of the existing Stone Hive the bixies constructed long ago on the eastern edge of Blightfire Moors. This one's much [more dangerous], though.'\nYou say, 'More dangerous?'\nJeslellathina holds a finger up to her lips and puts her ear to the ground, motioning for you to do the same. She asks, 'Do you hear that subtle thumping? It's been going non-stop ever since we discovered the cavern. The entire complex is a massive military wonderland: factories, battlefields, fortresses, training camps--they've got [everything] down there.'\nYou say, 'Everything?'\nJeslellathina says 'Everything. Including our friend, Jacyll. If you think you're up for the challenge, head down the ladder and speak to his brother, Frislo. He'll make sure you're [put to work] finding the stolen drakkin.'\nYou say, 'Put to work?'\nJeslellathina says 'Oh, yes. It's definitely work. Oh, wait. Are you accepting?' Jeslellathina doesn't wait for your response, immediately reciting, 'The people of Crescent Reach, and especially the family and friends of Jacyll thank you for your contribution. You may return to Crescent Reach for refreshments and possible dancing after Jacyll is rescued.'",
