      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Sarith, City of Tides [zone=808]\n**Who:**\n- Commander Marrien Kavus [npc=38387]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 91\n**Maximum Level:** | 95\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Arulien's Broken Sword [item=99826]\n- Counter Magic Scroll [item=99825]\n- Marinsi's Notebook [item=100167]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Guard Captain Naraind Reles [npc=38384]\n- Lieutenant Arulien [npc=38432]\n- Tidalmage Karith [npc=38434]\n- Tide Priest Marinsi [npc=38433]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Fri Nov 18 21:55:18 2011\nModified: Sun Aug 14 14:33:45 2022 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is a solo task that begins with Commander Marrien Kavus in Sarith (in the far northeastern part of the city at about 145, -845, -4)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- No tasks\n\\- 70 Skill Level in Alaran\n\n---\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Commander Marrien Kavus'\nCommander Marrien Kavus says, in Alaran, '\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_! I hope to you're here to help. If you're just here to ask questions, you're better off talking to my sibling, Ain. Al's got all the answers. I'm more into [acting] than talking.'\nYou say, 'Acting?'\nCommander Marrien Kavus says, in Alaran, 'That's what I'm talking about! There are a number of traitors that we need to deal with.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Unforgivable Betrayal'.\nMarrien Kavus needs your help in eliminating the traitors who have sided with the Orator's forces. Guard Captain Reles can provide you with information about where to look.\n\n---\n\nReceive instructions from Commander Marrien Kavus 0/1 (Sarith)\nYou say, 'Hail, Commander Marrien Kavus'\nCommander Marrien Kavus says, in Alaran, 'When the City of Bronze attacked, we didn't stand much of a chance. My sibling can give you more of the gory details. However, what made it worse are the people who betrayed us. I'm not just talking about those who followed Vyers after the occupation. I mean people who betrayed us while the fight was still going on. I want you to investigate a few areas and a few people. I have my suspicions, but I don't want to jump to conclusions. Here, take this list. Take notes. I want you to find the traitors, if you can.'\nQuestion Guard Captain Naraind Reles in their office 0/1 (Sarith)\n_The captain is found in the northwestern building (location 10, 620, 0)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Guard Captain Naraind Reles'\nGuard Captain Naraind Reles says, in Alaran, 'I see. Marrien has you looking into some of the problems we faced during the invasion? I can think of a few things that stand out. One: A number of our lookouts were assassinated, caught off guard. Very unusual. I suspect Lieutenant Arulien, as al is missing alir issued sword and has no alibi for alir location at the time, but have no proof. Two: We had a large rate of magical failure among our tidalmages and tide priests by the docks. Something went wrong there. Three: It seemed like many of our moves were anticipated, including our city park ambush. Riago Barthes is a genius, certainly, but al's not a mind reader. Someone leaked information to the enemy. Investigate these areas and people, and you may find the answers. I would help myself, but Eries keeps me under close watch. Good luck.'\n_This opens up the three sections below (each working essentially like a sub-task)._\n\n---\n\nInvestigate the docked ships 0/1 (Sarith)\n_This updates along the east side of the zone._\nLook for a counter-magic spell scroll on one of the docked ships 0/1 (Sarith)\n_Task Window Says:_ You found part of a counter-magic scroll. Look for the rest.\n_Counter Magic Scroll is at /waypoint -180, -704, -6 (on the railing of a small ship -- eastern dock on northwest side of the middle boat)._\nHunt down Tidalmage Karith 0/1 (Sarith)\n_Task Window Says:_ Confront the tidalmage who commanded the dock forces, Karith.\n_Tidalmage Karith is found in the far southern part of the dock area (around -710, -100). He is no more challenging than your average trash mob._\nTidalmage Karith has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nTidalmage Karith falls backwards, clutching their wounds. 'No! This wasn't supposed to happen! Riago promised I'd be safe if I helped.' Karith lets out a death rattle and topples backwards.\n\n---\n\nInvestigate the city park 0/1 (Sarith)\n_This updates in the southwest part of the zone._\nSearch the area around the park fountain for a discarded notebook 0/1 (Sarith)\n_Task Window Says:_ You found part of a map drawn in a book. Check the area around the city park fountain for the book.\n_Marinsi's Notebook is at -517, 484, -6 (just west of the fountain on the grass between two plants)._\nHunt down Tide Priest Marinsi 0/1 (Sarith)\n_Task Window Says:_ Inside the book was a hidden missive as well. The culprit is Tide Priest Marinsi.\n_Tide Priest Marinsi overlooks the residences in the southern part of the zone. He's found at about -625, 315 (average trash mob difficulty)._\nTide Priest Marinsi has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nTide Priest Marinsi coughs up some blood and wipes their mouth. 'So, are you really that short sighted? I did what I had to do. Oseka has returned, and I will not deny my true god. Oseka will protect me.' Myrinsi tries to stand, and fails, collapsing to the ground in a bloody heap.\n\n---\n\nSearch Lieutenant Arulien's room in the barracks 0/1 (Sarith)\n_Enter the building located northeast of Guard Captain Reles' building. Arulien's room is the first room on the right._\nSearch the waterfall pool for a discarded weapon 0/1 (Sarith)\n_Task Window Says:_ You found a note in Arulien's journal indicating the lookout's positions. They were mostly stationed around the waterfall. Check around there for Arulien's service weapon.\n_Arulien's Broken Sword is at 907, -80, -13 (behind the waterfall north of the city's main gate)._\nHunt down Lieutenant Arulien 0/1 (Sarith)\n_Task Window Says:_ You've found the sword used to kill the lookouts. Confront Arulien.\n_Lieutenant Arulien is found on the top side of the bridge, around -325, 25, 23. This fight is no more challenging than a trash mob._\nLieutenant Arulien has been slain by \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!\nLieutenant Arulien falls to one knee, bleeding heavily. 'So you figured it out? How? I don't care. I'd go it again! The City of Bronze is going to conquer everything, and I want to be on the winning side!' The Alaran tries to remain steady, but falls to the ground, unmoving.\n\n---\n\nDeliver the counter-magic scroll evidence to Commander Marrien Kavus 0/1 (Sarith)\nCommander Marrien Kavus says, in Alaran, 'Karith betrayed us? Heh, I guess I should not be surprised. Al was very ambitious. Dangerously so. This explains why the magic of the tides so often failed when cast by our mages ahd priests. Karith paid today for all their deaths.'\nDeliver the discarded notebook evidence to Commander Marrien Kavus 0/1 (Sarith)\nCommander Marrien Kavus says, in Alaran, 'Marinsi had been acting odd ever since news of the Orator from the City of Bronze reached our ears. It should not surprise me that al gave intelligence on our defensive efforts to the invading 'holy' army. I cannot forgive this. Thank you for taking care of Marinsi.'\nDeliver the missing weapon evidence to Commander Marrien Kavus 0/1 (Sarith)\nCommander Marrien Kavus says, in Alaran, 'I was afraid of this. I neven trusted ali. So shifty, so paranoid. When I saw ali disappear during the attack, I knew al was up to no good. Arulien got what he deserved for killing alir fellow guards and giving the City of Bronze a clear opening to the city.'\nTalk to Commander Marrien Kavus 0/1 (Sarith)\n_Task Window Says:_ Tidalmage Karith was responsible for the spell failures. Tide Priest Marinsi was responsible for the leaked intelligence. Lieutenant Arulien was responsible for the murdered scouts.\nYou say, 'Hail, Commander Marrien Kavus'\nCommander Marrien Kavus says, in Alaran, 'Thanks again for all your help. These three were responsible for a lot of innocent people's deaths when High Priest Vvers and Archon Eries attacked. Who knows whot further damage they could have done if they had been left alone.'\nYou've defeated the traitors who betrayed their own people and sold out Sarith to the City of Bronze. Marrien feels their people have been avenged, and Captain Reles appreciates your contribution to Sarith.\n_Rewards:_\n246 platinum\nEltarki's Diary - Time and Tides\n- Eltarki's Diary - Time and Tides [item=98630]",
    },
